{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1530510-player-created-conspiracies","id":1530510,"title":"Player Created Conspiracies?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-10T17:51:13-08:00","id":1530510,"title":"Player Created Conspiracies?","content":"Got a one on one session with another player. We\u2019re doing Demon and they want to take the Cultist Merit, but expand it globally. I thought \u201cthat sounds more like a conspiracy than a cult.\u201d So my question: would it be possible for a player to CREATE their own conspiracy and if so, how do I do it mechanically?<br /> <br /> keep in mind they\u2019re playing a Demon so they can use pacts, I just need a bit of help with the design mechanics. Or ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T18:18:54-08:00","id":1530517,"title":"","content":"Mechanics for creating a conspiracy in-game are included in the Devoted Companion and involve creating and/or taking control of enough Nodes to meet the minimums for Standing 1.<br /> <br /> This is notably different from having cults of the sort the Unchained and the God-Machine use operate at that level; as Demon Core describes it, the God-Machine typically sticks to small cults due to greater risk of discovery, and the Unchained suffer worse consequences from the same risks. Demons mostly manage to have the level of influence a cult represents through the Merit, Social Merits, and/or using the Tempter Agenda Condition \u2014 Cultists specifically doesn't measure how large your cult is, so the effects don't really scale any differently.<br /> <br /> You'd likely be slightly better-served modeling this in line with the more player-facing organization mechanics found in Geist or Mummy, though in any game a global-scale cult is high-level stuff beyond the reach of a starting character without addressing the kind of exceptions that put that in their grasp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T18:34:26-08:00","id":1530519,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Of the two, I'd probably recommend MtC's Cults, as they aren't quite as bound up in the underlying game's specific metaphysics as Geist's krewe rules are. In particular, Mummy's Cults <i>assume</i> that their membership will include a diverse selection of beings, and not just Mummy-specific stuff. Having demons in the mix wouldn't be all that unusual; and the only unusual thing about what you're doing would be the <i>lack</i> of a mummy in the Cult's power structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T05:07:58-08:00","id":1530545,"title":"","content":"lol. I find it funny that out of the 12 \u2018templates\u2019, my solution just so happens to be in the ONE book I have NOT properly read. (The Mummy one)<br /> <br /> Thanks guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}